From 50ac245149eaf66462e0a96109c9bb97afd92968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhanraj <dp914278@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:38:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] window: Add complete native per-tab dual-pane navigation

Wrap each tab page in a NautilusWindowTab with two real browse slots. Keep
one weak active slot as shared toolbar/sidebar/action authority and isolate
inactive managed shortcuts. F3 creates Home as the new pane location;
Ctrl+W closes the focused pane and promotes its sibling.

Include floating native card islands, rounded clipping, unclipped outer
shadows, measured drag/window limits, proportional resizing and translation
registration. Normalize incomplete close records, preserve valid histories,
and restore post-promotion or ordinary reuse focus without stealing shared
entry/background focus. Bind child callbacks to tab lifetime and dispose
template state safely. No incremental feature-fix patches are required.

Activate a split pane on pointer hover when no edit, popup/dialog, held
button or drag is in progress. Keep keyboard context on the same pane
without fighting a stationary pointer. Make the inactive surface recede
and dim its file content while preserving native shadows and geometry.
---
